    "_comment_rotary_geo": "── Rotary (4th-axis). SPLIT RULE: a key gets its own indexed* entry only when the QUANTITY DIFFERS IN KIND - rotaryRoughStepdown is radius-per-layer, indexedRoughStepdown is Z-per-layer. Stepover %, stock, resolution, tool shape, pass mode, axis offsets AND the workholding set (rotaryHoldingMode, rotaryChuck/TailEnd*, rotaryMinRadius) mean the same thing in both engines and stay SHARED on the rotary* key - both handlers read them through ShapeRotaryHandler.resolveWorkholding, the single interpretation point. Chuck = LOW end of the rotary axis, tail = HIGH end, both kinematics. Direction keys are semantic ('axial'/'cross'), resolved per machine axis in ShapeIndexedHandler.axialGridAxis. indexedAngles (custom list) still waits on a text-input field type. evaluateConditionals only sets display:none - a hidden parameter keeps its value and still reaches the handler through the merged bag; the pair that must never be confused is rotaryRoughStepdown (radial, radius) vs indexedRoughStepdown (indexed, Z). indexedCollisionGuard needs settings.tool, which only exists once a rotary tool select is added.",

    "rotaryToolShape": {
      "type": "select",
      "label": "Tool Tip Shape",
      "stage": "geometry",
      "category": "tool",
      "operationTypes": "rotary",
      "default": "ball",
      "options": [
        { "value": "ball", "label": "Ball Nose" },
        { "value": "flat", "label": "Flat Endmill" },
        { "value": "bull", "label": "Bull Nose (corner radius)" }
      ]
    },
